git
===

g is an alias for git.

BASICS
  g la                            List all aliases
  g s                             status
  g cim "msg"                     commit -m
  g ac "msg"                      add . and commit -am
  g cob x                         checkout -b x
  g brD x                         branch -D x
  g com                           Check out the default branch (master, main or mainline,
                                  from origin/HEAD)
  g default-branch                Print the default branch (git remote set-head origin
                                  --auto if it is wrong)
  gr                              cd to the repo root (zsh alias)

DIFF AND LOG
  g d / g dc                      diff / diff --cached
  g dlc                           Diff of the last commit (--cached HEAD^)
  g dr <sha>                      Diff of one commit
  g code-review                   difftool against origin/<default branch>
  g lg                            log --oneline --graph
  g ls / g ll                     Log, one line / with file stats
  g ld / g lds                    Log with relative / short dates

RESET AND LOCAL EDITS
  g r1 / g rh1                    reset HEAD^ (soft) / --hard
  g assume <f> / g unassume <f>   Hide / show local edits to a tracked file
  g assumed                       List hidden files

BRANCHES AND REMOTES
  g publish                       push -u origin <current branch>
  g unpublish                     Delete the remote copy of the current branch
  g delete-merged-branches        Check out the default branch and delete branches merged
                                  into it
  g delete-untracked-branches     Fetch and prune origin
  gh:user/repo                    URL shorthand for https://github.com/user/repo
